  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Etoduma</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Etoduma SARL is an agri-food company that processes locally grown plantains and sweet potatoes into chips. The project aims to improve the productivity and product quality of Etodumas products to better meet the demands of the Ivorian market for plantain and sweet potato chips. USADF funds will cover the following expenses: 1) slicing and peeling equipment; 2) draining equipment;.3) bagging machine; 4) irrigation equipment; 5) working capital for the purchase of plantains and sweet.potatoes; 6) packaging for Chips; 7) working capital for plantain input; 8) training on USADF rules and.regulations; 9) training in best production practices; 10) local and international food quality certification;.11) accounting staff; 12) training of producers on good agricultural practices; 13) marketing and sales.assistance; and 14) IT equipment.</narrative>
  </description>
